course: dictionary
lesson: 13433
title: Words with two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You can tell which one the author means by reading the words around it. «The school held an assembly honouring the nurses who helped our town.» The clues are assembly and nurses, so honouring means showing great respect.
explain: The same word can mean something different in another sentence. «Ben said he would meet me at four, and he came at four, honouring his promise.» There is no ceremony here. Ben kept his promise, so honouring means keeping a promise.
explain: Ask yourself: what is the big clue? An assembly, an award or a hero points to respect. A promise or a word points to keeping an agreement. Then swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Honour is a verb, and honouring is its -ing form.
fact: «Honouring» means showing great respect to someone, often in a ceremony or with an award.
fact: «Honouring» can also mean keeping a promise or agreement, as in «honouring your word».
fact: In American English the spelling is honoring, without the u.
fact: The same word can have more than one meaning, so always check the context.
exercise: «The town is honouring its local heroes with a parade.» What is the town doing? | *Showing great respect to its heroes | Closing the park | Forgetting its heroes | Building a new road
exercise: «She kept her word, honouring the promise she made to her friend.» What does honouring mean here? | Forgetting the promise | Shouting at her friend | *Keeping the promise | Breaking a window
exercise: «The school held a ceremony, honouring the soldiers.» Which word is the best clue that honouring means showing respect? | soldiers | *ceremony | held | school
test: «Dad is honouring his promise to take me swimming on Saturday.» What does honouring mean here? | Forgetting his promise | Cancelling the trip | *Keeping his promise | Shouting at the pool
test: «The mayor gave a medal, honouring the brave firefighter.» What does honouring mean here? | Keeping a promise | Hiding the medal | *Showing great respect | Losing the firefighter
exam: Jayden reads «honouring your word» and «honouring our heroes». Why do the two sentences mean different things? | Honouring always means exactly the same thing | One sentence is longer than the other | *The clues are different, so the meaning changes with the context | One sentence is from a story and the other is not
